<blockquote>
<p>at first i thought about making it an investigate format story about trying crack this SCP about its origins and the reason why it goes around attacking mining factories</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is actually something you'll want to focus on no matter what you do with this; an entity that attacks mining facilities is a generic monster. An entity with an origin grounded in the mythology of the region that has an understandable reason for attacking mining facilities (preferably with some unexpected twists along the way) is a character.</p>
<p>Specifically, I'd focus on the aspect of what turns this entity against the mines- it's fairly easy to have it simply be angry about the mining boom in Mongolia, but what if it's not about the mines per-say? In the days of the Khans, Mongolia was the largest empire on Earth, and today those mines have the potential to return a measure of that glory- provided Mongolia isn't cut out of its own harvest.</p>

